                            <comment id="16010035" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 15 May 2017 06:45:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;, could you please clarify how this was fixed? Did it require any changes to the protocol?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16010107" author="ptupitsyn" created="Mon, 15 May 2017 07:40:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vozerov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vozerov&quot;&gt;vozerov&lt;/a&gt; no changes to the protocol.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Enums can be &lt;tt&gt;byte&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;sbyte&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;short&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;ushort&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;int&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;uint&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;long&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;ulong&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In 2.0 there is an exception for any non-&lt;tt&gt;int&lt;/tt&gt; enum.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;After this fix all enums that fit into 4 bytes are written in Ignite format. &lt;tt&gt;long&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;ulong&lt;/tt&gt; enums are written as regular objects with a single field (via reflective serializer).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
